  "Parts are the same as step 1; none added or dropped.",
  "Board is an Arduino Leonardo, as in the schematic. The circuit photo did not load, so the layout is my own, built from the schematic.",
  "Each pushbutton straddles the centre gap. Side 1 (1.l, 1.r) is in the top half, in columns c and c+2, and goes to the 5V rail (tp) through a jumper wire. Side 2 (2.l, 2.r) is in the bottom half. The Leonardo pin wire and one leg of the 10k pulldown share the bottom-half strip of column c. The resistor's other leg goes to the GND rail (bn). The buttons use columns 3, 7, 11, 15 and 19.",
  "Pin mapping follows the tutorial: D2 up, D3 down, D4 left, D5 right, D6 mouse click.",
  "Leonardo 5V goes to rail tp and GND.1 goes to rail bn. The micro-USB cable has no named ports on either side, so it has a single joined edge to the board."
